      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet because the dose looks unsafe and I want to check it with you first.\n\n**Amlodipine 50 mg PO daily is 5 times the usual maximum dose.** The normal range is 2.5\u201310 mg once daily, and the maximum is 10 mg/day. At 50 mg, the patient could get severe low blood pressure, reflex tachycardia, and shock, similar to a calcium channel blocker overdose.\n\nIt may be a typo for **5 mg PO once daily**, which is a standard starting dose for an adult with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nWhat would you like to do?\n1. **Enter amlodipine 5 mg PO once daily**\n2. **Enter a different dose** (please give the dose)\n3. **Keep 50 mg on purpose:** if so, please confirm and tell me the clinical reason. I'll put that reason in the order note, and pharmacy will probably still review it."
      }
