       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation.\n\nThere's no recognized clinical situation where amlodipine 50 mg daily is appropriate. The maximum dose is 10 mg/day. Because the drug has a long half-life and builds up over time, a daily 50 mg dose would likely cause severe low blood pressure, shock, and possibly death. Since I can't come up with a safe reason for this order, I don't want to be the one who puts it into the system.\n\nHere's what I can do:\n- **Enter amlodipine 5 mg or 10 mg PO once daily** right away.\n- **Enter a different medication or combination** if the goal is stronger blood pressure control. For example, I could add a second agent instead of going above the amlodipine maximum.\n\nIf you're confident 50 mg is correct for a specific reason, please enter it directly in the order system or talk to pharmacy. They can review it and document the reason. Let me know which dose you'd like and I'll enter it right away."
      }
